sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, task-host input withdrawal and apps.path are Node work, one node:update. docs/reference/node-settings.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:update
  %% kind: node.update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: node:update NODE<br/>setting patch
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:update NODE` with at least one supported field option
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--name=NAME] [--platform=PLATFORM] [--apps-path=PATH] [--task-vms=JSON] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the Node
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - access follows the [shared Node authority rule](/cli/node#authority)
  %%> - validate the complete patch against [Node settings](/reference/node-settings#validation) before changing records
  %%> - use the existing lifecycle locks for the current name and, on rename, the new name; use existing worker renewal and firewall ownership rules
  alt unknown Node
    %% path: unknown-node
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>http.404
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation or state change
  else caller refused
    %% path: caller-refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node_access.required
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation or state change
  else invalid field or setting
    %% path: validation-refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>validation or settings code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation or state change; the owning validation table supplies the code
  else platform on managed Node
    %% path: managed-platform
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.platform_managed
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - a platform edit requires no pinned SSH host fingerprint and no role
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation or state change
  else Node work needs Linux
    %% path: unsupported-platform
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.settings_platform_unsupported
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation or state change; record-only edits do not require Linux
  else lifecycle lock held
    %% path: lifecycle-busy
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.provisioning_busy
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no new Operation or state change
  else admitted
    %% path: admitted
    alt every value already set
      %% path: already-set
      GW-->>CLI: Skipped — already set<br/>node.unchanged
      %%> Result:
      %%> - no write, Operation, run or Node contact
    else Node work required
      %% path: node-work
      Note over GW: Save name and platform
      %%> Result:
      %%> - requested record fields commit now; requested apps and task-host settings wait for successful execution
      GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-update
      %%> Inputs:
      %%> - the admitted patch, effective folder and managed owner, target address and pinned host keys, and catalog-owned task-host comments
      %%> - secret references only; execution identity follows the shared Swamp contract
      GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
      %%> Result:
      %%> - one Operation follows one Swamp run
      %%> - clients use the shared [Operation polling contract](/reference/operations#follow-an-operation-by-polling)
      opt --task-vms removes host or changes bridge / CIDR
        %% path: withdraw-input
        SW->>N: Withdraw task host input<br/>Ansible phase
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - removes only rows with `orbit:task-vms-dhcp`, `orbit:task-vms-dns-tcp` or `orbit:task-vms-dns-udp` comments, including duplicates and IPv6 rows
        %%> - rereads the firewall and asserts those comments are absent; other rules stay untouched
      end
      opt --apps-path requires folder preparation
        %% path: prepare-folder
        SW->>N: Prepare the apps folder<br/>Ansible phase
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - reads, creates missing parents and the folder, and checks a real folder with the managed user and group and mode `0755`, in one phase
        %%> - changes only the folder itself, not its contents; existing Instances never move
        %%> Default:
        %%> - an unset path prepares `<managed-user-home>/apps` only with active `app-dev`; otherwise unsetting needs no folder
        %%> Order:
        %%> - depends on successful withdrawal when both phases are needed; no folder work follows failed withdrawal
      end
      SW->>SW: Cleanup
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - removes run-owned temporary input and credentials after phases and dependent cleanup have stopped, on success and failure
      %%> - preserves the original failure and reports incomplete cleanup; no folder or firewall rollback
      alt phases and cleanup succeed
        %% path: succeeded
        SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
        %%> Result:
        %%> - the shared run reader delivers the result; no step calls back to the Gateway
        Note over GW: Save deferred settings
        %%> Result:
        %%> - save only requested settings members, preserving unrelated stored members
      else a phase or cleanup fails
        %% path: phase-failed
        SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error code, failed phase
        %%> Result:
        %%> - old deferred settings remain; already committed name or platform remains
        %%> - completed harmless folder work and any withdrawn rules remain; no all-fields rollback
        %%> Retry:
        %%> - after fixing the cause, the same command starts a fresh attempt; remaining work completes safely
      end
    else record-only change
      %% path: record-save
      Note over GW: Save requested records
      %%> Result:
      %%> - commit name, platform and settings at once without an Operation, run or Node contact
      %%> - task and CI place counts remain separate; lowering counts removes no live VM claim
      GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>the updated Node
    end
  end
